{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "`tautline merge` accepts a caller-supplied `--match-head-commit` again in every case where the gate has nothing to substitute for it. 0.35.1 refused it UNCONDITIONALLY: the flag sat in the protected-passthrough set, screened before enforcement was even read, so `mergeGate.enforcement=off` -- which reads no rollup at all -- refused the caller's pin while offering none of its own. The condition that matters is whether the gate actually HOLDS a verified head, which is also false with enforcement advise or block and an UNVERIFIABLE rollup, where the verb proceeds by design. In all of those the refusal stripped gh's own race protection and replaced it with nothing. It now fires only when a verified head exists, which is the only case where a caller pin could silently swap in a commit nothing classified.",
    "The registrar-carve shape pin asserts exactly what it did before -- every add_parser call inside a _register_<family>_<n> segment, nesting included -- and was proven non-vacuous by planting a stray add_parser in main() and confirming the rewritten test still fails.",
    "The suite's single slowest test drops from 35.56s to 0.85s. On an xdist worker a 35s test is a floor no other worker can lower, so the gain is largest where the worker count is smallest -- which is CI."
  ],
